<title>UK: Moody's may cut Banca Popolare di Verona.</title>
<headline>Moody's may cut Banca Popolare di Verona.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's rating agency said on Wednesday it had placed under review for possible downgrade the A1 long-term deposit rating, A1 counterparty rating and C plus bank financial strength rating of Banca Popolare di Verona-Banco San Geminiano e San Prospero (BPV).</p>
<p>It said the action followed the announcement the bank is to acquire Credit Lyonnais' 57 percent stake in Credito Bergamasco at a price of 35,400 lira per share.  </p>
<p>Moody's said BPV would be required to make an offer to remaining shareholders at the same price, valuing Credito Bergamasco at 2.2 trillion lire, compared with a book value of 1.0 trillion.</p>
